        "body": "## Summary\n- Add `codexbar cards`, a one-shot terminal usage snapshot with a responsive provider card grid.\n- Add `codexbar cards --brief`, a compact Provider / Usage / Reset table with source/plan detail and enhanced terminal colors.\n- Reuse the existing `codexbar usage` fetch pipeline, summarize provider failures in a footer, and document the new command.\n\n## Screenshots\n![Card grid](https://github.com/DonnieFi/CodexBar/blob/feat/cli-cards/codexbar_cards_clean.png?raw=true)\n\n![Brief table](https://github.com/DonnieFi/CodexBar/blob/feat/cli-cards/codexbar_cards_brief.png?raw=true)\n\n## Test plan\n- `swift test --filter 'CLICards|CLITerminalCapabilities'`\n- `swift build --product CodexBarCLI -c release`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `make check` reaches SwiftFormat cleanly, then fails on this Linux host when SwiftLint/SourceKit cannot load `libsourcekitdInProc.so`.\n\n## Notes\n- `Package.resolved` is intentionally unchanged; macOS-only dependencies are gated in `Package.swift` to avoid Linux CLI dependency noise.\n- Kitty/Ghostty/WezTerm/truecolor terminals auto-enable enhanced cards, with `CODEXBAR_CARDS_ENHANCED` as an override.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
